WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.540
Hurricane Audrey in 1957 came through this country and overnight we had big open water areas where the dead saw grass had been swept off.

2
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:18.660
And some technical papers showed up that the storms scoured it out.

3
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:26.540
Hell, it was dead and was just sitting there waiting for something to transport it, which Audrey did.

4
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:40.560
But today we can't possibly restore these marshes out here without getting the water off of the surface.

5
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:47.240
Over the length of time that has occurred since Hurricane Audrey in '57 and today,

6
00:00:47.240 --> 00:01:02.060
we've had millions of tons silt . . . of detrital material, or old decomposed marsh material floated out of here with outgoing tides.

7
00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:11.160
So, to get a surface out there where plants can grow again is either through mechanical dredging and fill,

8
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:20.240
or through some kind of a massive drawdown of water out of these areas through pumping or gravity draining.

9
00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:32.040
Well, you get into that, you're talking about huge, huge amounts of money to get the stage to be able to grow grass again.

10
00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.180
Well what are you going to get out of that grass you grow?

11
00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:38.220
You can't graze cows out in there,

12
00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:45.480
you can't sell grass seed for human food except wheat and corn and some of those . . . Well,

13
00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.220
that ain't going to grow out here.

14
00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:58.340
So there's no economic incentive or need to try and rebuild these marshes except for storm protection.
